  "worked_solution": "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}$ is a line segment that \n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $C$ to the line $\\overset{\u27f7}{AB},$ and\n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{\u27f7}{AB}.$\n\nTo draw the height, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Extend the line segment $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945712/assets/eba964fd799b57b787ab20955b8717b02219ed785d2455cb122e08c448b43563.png)\n\n- Draw the perpendicular from $C$ to $\\overset{\u27f7}{AB}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945712/assets/adc7bbe174cdc56b7146d85bdec6e568e2cf829a3a64c73f6555e62c168c2eeb.png)",
